            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Poetry and Human Rights</strong><br>\nHugo's poetry, like his novels, focused on social issues and human rights. His collections, such as \"Les Contemplations\" and \"La Légende des siècles,\" reflect his advocacy for the oppressed and his philosophical ruminations on humanity.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Family Tragedy</strong><br>\nPersonal tragedy struck with the untimely death of his daughter Léopoldine, which deeply affected Hugo. His grief profoundly influenced his later works, where themes of loss and mourning are prevalent.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nVictor Hugo died in 1885 and was given a national funeral. He is remembered as a literary colossus whose works have inspired countless readers and writers worldwide. His burial in the Panthéon in Paris solidified his status as a French national icon.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
